  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Harnessing Youth Leadership and Improving Education Outcomes in the Middle East</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Middle East Regional (MER)):  The Harnessing Youth Leadership to Improve Education Outcomes Activity is a $2.4 million program implemented by Teach for All (TFALL) that channels youth leadership towards strengthening and promoting education for children in the Middle East region. TFALL provides university graduates opportunities to support classroom-based and non-formal learning, such as providing remedial support. The organization will also help to launch and grow locally-rooted, national organizations that enlist their nation&apos;s most promising young leaders in a two-year foundational and skill-building classroom teaching experience that increases student access to learning opportunities. These newly launched organizations will work in partnership with local communities and government officials to foster sustainable changes to the education systems. USAID assistance will continue support for Teach for Morocco and expand Teach for Lebanon&apos;s efforts to reach high-need students (including refugees), improve capacity to measure results, and function as a model approach to other organizations in the region. ..TFALL will also support prospective partners in the Middle East to launch new network programs in Tunisia by providing direct support to early stage entrepreneurs working towards adapting the approach for deployment in Tunisia; and to illustrate the core approach that other organizations are pursuing throughout the world. Key components of this approach include: the sharing of global resources (i.e. tools, templates and more); setting up virtual calls/video chats and facilitating peer to peer connections.  ..This mechanism will program $360,000 towards the Basic Education earmark and $100,000 towards Basic Education for Girls in Conflict... .. .</narrative>
  </description>
